arguments.prompt:
You are implementing a Blazor Web App for a logistics company that tracks shipments. The project is already scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-f57d27c5f49447cf9cacf89d642833ba/ShipmentTracker/` with Interactive Auto, Global mode and Individual authentication.

Project structure:
- `ShipmentTracker/` - server project
- `ShipmentTracker.Client/` - client/WebAssembly project

Key architecture rules for Auto Global mode:
- All interactive components MUST go in the `.Client` project
- Interactive components cannot access DB directly — use HTTP APIs
- Define service interfaces in `.Client`, implement with HttpClient there, implement with direct data access in server
- Register matching services in both Program.cs files
- Don't add `@rendermode` to pages (global mode handles it)
- Identity/Account pages must stay static SSR (don't touch them)

## Tasks

### 1. Remove template pages
Delete these files from `ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/`:
- `Counter.razor`
- `Weather.razor`

### 2. Create shared models
Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Exception
}
```

### 3. Create service interface in Client project
Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string customerEmail);
    Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status);
}
```

### 4. Create Client-side implementation (uses HttpClient)
Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentServiceClient.cs`:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ShipmentServiceClient(HttpClient http) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>("api/shipments") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        return await http.GetFromJsonAsync<Shipment?>($"api/shipments/track/{trackingNumber}");
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string customerEmail)
    {
        return await http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>($"api/shipments/customer/{Uri.EscapeDataString(customerEmail)}") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        await http.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", status);
    }
}
```

### 5. Create Server-side implementation (direct data access with in-memory store for demo)
Create `ShipmentTracker/Services/ShipmentServiceServer.cs`:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Services;

public class ShipmentServiceServer : IShipmentService
{
    private static readonly List<Shipment> _shipments = new()
    {
        new() { Id = 1, TrackingNumber = "TRK-001-2026", Origin = "New York, US", Destination = "London, UK", Status = ShipmentStatus.InTransit, EstimatedDelivery = DateTime.Today.AddDays(3), ShippedDate = DateTime.Today.AddDays(-2), CustomerEmail = "alice@example.com", Description = "Electronics - 2 boxes" },
        new() { Id = 2, TrackingNumber = "TRK-002-2026", Origin = "Shanghai, CN", Destination = "Los Angeles, US", Status = ShipmentStatus.PickedUp, EstimatedDelivery = DateTime.Today.AddDays(10), ShippedDate = DateTime.Today.AddDays(-1), CustomerEmail = "bob@example.com", Description = "Furniture - 1 pallet" },
        new() { Id = 3, TrackingNumber = "TRK-003-2026", Origin = "Berlin, DE", Destination = "Tokyo, JP", Status = ShipmentStatus.OutForDelivery, EstimatedDelivery = DateTime.Today, ShippedDate = DateTime.Today.AddDays(-5), CustomerEmail = "carol@example.com", Description = "Auto parts - 5 crates" },
        new() { Id = 4, TrackingNumber = "TRK-004-2026", Origin = "Sydney, AU", Destination = "Mumbai, IN", Status = ShipmentStatus.Delivered, EstimatedDelivery = DateTime.Today.AddDays(-1), ShippedDate = DateTime.Today.AddDays(-7), CustomerEmail = "alice@example.com", Description = "Medical supplies - 3 boxes" },
        new() { Id = 5, TrackingNumber = "TRK-005-2026", Origin = "São Paulo, BR", Destination = "Miami, US", Status = ShipmentStatus.Exception, EstimatedDelivery = DateTime.Today.AddDays(2), ShippedDate = DateTime.Today.AddDays(-3), CustomerEmail = "dave@example.com", Description = "Textiles - 10 boxes" },
        new() { Id = 6, TrackingNumber = "TRK-006-2026", Origin = "Dubai, AE", Destination = "Paris, FR", Status = ShipmentStatus.Pending, EstimatedDelivery = DateTime.Today.AddDays(6), ShippedDate = DateTime.Today, CustomerEmail = "bob@example.com", Description = "Machinery - 2 containers" },
    };

    private static int _nextId = 7;

    public Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return Task.FromResult(_shipments.ToList());
    }

    public Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        var shipment = _shipments.FirstOrDefault(s =>
            s.TrackingNumber.Equals(trackingNumber, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase));
        return Task.FromResult(shipment);
    }

    public Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string customerEmail)
    {
        var results = _shipments
            .Where(s => s.CustomerEmail.Equals(customerEmail, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
            .ToList();
        return Task.FromResult(results);
    }

    public Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        var shipment = _shipments.FirstOrDefault(s => s.Id == id);
        if (shipment is not null)
        {
            shipment.Status = status;
        }
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }
}
```

### 6. Create API endpoints
Create `ShipmentTracker/ShipmentEndpoints.cs`:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

namespace ShipmentTracker;

public static class ShipmentEndpoints
{
    public static void MapShipmentApi(this WebApplication app)
    {
        var group = app.MapGroup("api/shipments").RequireAuthorization();

        group.MapGet("/", async (IShipmentService service) =>
            await service.GetAllShipmentsAsync());

        group.MapGet("/track/{trackingNumber}", async (string trackingNumber, IShipmentService service) =>
        {
            var shipment = await service.GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(trackingNumber);
            return shipment is not null ? Results.Ok(shipment) : Results.NotFound();
        });

        group.MapGet("/customer/{email}", async (string email, IShipmentService service) =>
            await service.GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(email));

        group.MapPut("/{id}/status", async (int id, ShipmentStatus status, IShipmentService service) =>
        {
            await service.UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(id, status);
            return Results.NoContent();
        });
    }
}
```

### 7. Update Server Program.cs
In `ShipmentTracker/Program.cs`, add these registrations. Add `using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;` and `using ShipmentTracker.Services;` and `using ShipmentTracker;` at the top.

After the existing service registrations (after `AddSingleton<IEmailSender...>` line), add:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentServiceServer>();
```

Before `app.Run();`, add:
```csharp
app.MapShipmentApi();
```

### 8. Update Client Program.cs
In `ShipmentTracker.Client/Program.cs`, add the HttpClient and service registration. The final file should be:
```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Hosting;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

var builder = WebAssemblyHostBuilder.CreateDefault(args);

builder.Services.AddAuthorizationCore();
builder.Services.AddCascadingAuthenticationState();
builder.Services.AddAuthenticationStateDeserialization();

builder.Services.AddScoped(sp => new HttpClient { BaseAddress = new Uri(builder.HostEnvironment.BaseAddress) });
builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentServiceClient>();

await builder.Build().RunAsync();
```

### 9. Create Pages

#### Update Home.razor (`ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Home.razor`):
